'''Southshore''' (or '''South Shore''')<ref>''World of Warcraft: Game Manual''</ref> is an [[Alliance]] port town located in the region of [[Hillsbrad Foothills]]. It is a quiet port town and one of the few pockets of human civilization that existed in Lordaeron, maintaining their allegiance to the [[Alliance]]. A few survivors of the Third War and adventurers call this town home.

==History==
===Second War===
After fleeing the [[Old Horde|Horde]] which had destroyed their kingdom during the [[First War]], the refugees of [[Stormwind (kingdom)|Azeroth]] settled near Southshore, pledging their loyalty to the recently formed [[Alliance of Lordaeron|Alliance]].<ref>''Warcraft II: Tides of Darkness'' manual, ''[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/Warcraft_II:_Tides_of_Darkness_manual#Azeroth Nations of the Alliance]'', Azeroth</ref> Southshore was transformed into a busy seaport during the [[Second War]].<ref>[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/Southshore_(WC2_Human) Southshore (WC2 Human)]</ref> Its maritime area was rich with oil, which was also coveted by the Horde.<ref>[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/Southshore_(WC2_Orc) Southshore (WC2 Orc)]</ref>

Despite its new status as a military port, Southshore was eventually attacked and taken by the rampaging Horde.<ref>[https://wowpedia.fandom.com/wiki/Tol_Barad_(WC2_Human) Tol Barad (WC2 Human)]</ref> Sometime after the war, Southshore was rebuilt by the Alliance.

